description:
Add docs/design/character-creation-cli.md capturing the agreed character creation UX and architecture.

The document must preserve the full design rather than summarize it away. It should cover:
- one shared CLI shell with rule-pack-specific character creation recipes;
- D&D 5e SRD as the first recipe;
- future Pathfinder compatibility without speculative Pathfinder implementation;
- canonical mode labels: Concept-first — I know what I want to play, and Ability-first — let the dice inspire me;
- why both modes matter: modern concept-first play plus 80s-era RPG nostalgia/discovery play;
- concept-first and ability-first step orders;
- shared commands: ?, list, search <term>, back, review, set <field>, save, quit;
- forgiving display-name/common-alias input;
- stateful draft preservation and save/resume behavior;
- dependency-aware validation with actionable diagnostics and no cascades;
- automatic derived values, especially level-1 HP;
- runtime generated rules-pack resolver replacing SRD_CATALOG;
- likely need for structured choice metadata beyond prose records;
- proposed components: RulesPackCharacterResolver, CharacterCreationRecipe, CharacterCreationDraft, CharacterCreationEngine, CharacterCreationCli;
- implementation slices, acceptance criteria, non-goals, and ADR candidate decisions.

Acceptance criteria
- Design doc exists in the repo.
- Open beads eshyra-4jiu and eshyra-x50w are referenced as inputs/overlaps.
- The doc is explicit that this PR is design/planning only and does not implement runtime behavior.
